% ADJ52 case-28 program (this patient's observations + queries only; no rules).
% 59-year-old man, ~10 weeks of crampy lower abdominal pain, bloating, audible
% borborygmi, loose pale-yellow stools 4x/day, ~18 kg unintentional weight loss
% (malabsorption); new numbness of hands and feet with EMG/NCS-confirmed active
% peripheral neuropathy; spontaneous bruise-like patches + petechiae over forearms
% and shins (no trauma); MACROGLOSSIA on exam. Laparotomy for presumed peritonitis:
% 180 mL dark blood-tinged fluid, NO perforation, cecum-to-ileum diffusely swollen,
% edematous, firm and granular; diffuse small-bowel wall thickening on imaging.
% Labs: Hb 86, albumin 22 (markedly low), creatinine 205, urinalysis 2+ protein
% with micro-haematuria/pyuria, 24h urine protein 910 mg (sub-nephrotic), ESR 52,
% CRP 188 (markedly elevated), IL-6 47 (elevated), procalcitonin mildly raised,
% GGT/ALP mildly raised; TSH 21 with low-normal free T4 (primary hypothyroidism);
% hs-troponin-T 20, NT-proBNP 910; cardiac MRI small lateral-wall myocardial
% signal change WITHOUT wall thickening. Clonal/monoclonal workup THOROUGHLY
% NEGATIVE: serum + urine immunofixation negative, Bence-Jones absent, serum free
% light chains normal, immunoglobulins/CTD panel unremarkable, serum VEGF normal,
% marrow non-clonal with mild (7%) plasmacytosis. No unifying diagnosis yet.
% Amyloid tissue typing and TTR sequencing PENDING.

% --- the shared amyloid infiltrative tissue syndrome (one deposition process) ---
observe bowel_infiltration(firm_granular)
observe macroglossia(present)
observe purpura(spontaneous_nontraumatic)
observe proteinuria(sub_nephrotic)
observe peripheral_neuropathy(active)
observe cardiac_signal_change(present)

% --- the acute-phase / SAA-driving inflammatory signature ---
observe crp(markedly_elevated)
observe il6(elevated)
observe esr(elevated)

% --- independent type-discriminating findings ---
observe clonal_workup(fully_negative)
observe vegf(normal)
observe renal_predominant(present)
observe demographic(older_male)

% NOT observed (open, decision-relevant — these are the pending tests):
%   amyloid_typing(serum_amyloid_a) vs amyloid_typing(immunoglobulin_light_chain)
%     vs amyloid_typing(transthyretin)
%   ttr_gene(pathogenic_variant) vs ttr_gene(no_variant)

